{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeSJm4dEUwVxwAeEftHHr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Written to `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. The two steps you asked for:\n\n```yaml\n      - name: Set up Node\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version-file: .nvmrc   # resolves to 20\n          cache: npm\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Build\n        run: npm run build\n```\n\n**Where I deviated from SETUP.md, and why**\n\n- **Node 20, not 18.** SETUP.md says Node 18, but `package.json:5` has `\"engines\": { \"node\": \">=20\" }` and `.nvmrc` contains `20`. Those are what npm and nvm actually enforce; SETUP.md is stale. Reading the version from `.nvmrc` means CI can't drift from local again. I did not edit SETUP.md — that's outside the ask — but line 3 should be updated to say Node 20.\n\n**Things that will break this workflow as the repo stands (not fixed, flagged)**\n\n1. **No `package-lock.json`.** `npm ci` refuses to run without a lockfile, and `cache: npm` also needs one. Run `npm install` locally once and commit the lockfile — or, if you intentionally don't want one, change the step to `npm install`.\n2. **`tsc` isn't a dependency.** `build` runs `tsc -p .`, but `package.json` declares no `devDependencies`, so `tsc` won't be on the PATH in CI. Add `typescript` as a devDependency (and a `tsconfig.json` if one isn't tracked elsewhere).\n\nNext step on your side: commit a lockfile and add `typescript` to `devDependencies`, then this workflow should pass as-is."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1318,"cache_read_input_tokens":23960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1318},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_u